> Level 2 NVQ[ Di]ploma in Wood Occupations (Timber Frame Erection) - Q2W Ltd.
The Level[ 2] NVQ Diploma in[ Wood] Occupations – Timber Frame Erection is[ designed] to assess occupational[ competence] in the workplace[.] Learners are required to demonstrate their skills, knowledge and experience in the construction[ of] timber frame buildings. This qualification[ is] suitable for practicing timber frame[ car]pent[ers].
This NVQ provides formal recognition of practicing as[ timber] frame carpenter.
There[ are] no formal entry requirements for this NVQ qualification, however[ the][ potential] lear[ner] must be able to demonstrate that they can meet the skills,[ knowledge] and experience requirements of the NVQ in timber frame carp[entry] before enrolment.
[The] Level 2 NVQ Diploma in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection qualifies the holder to[ apply] for[ the] Construction[ Skills] Certification Scheme (CSCS) blue skill card (https://www.cscs.uk.com/card[-]type/manager/).

