> [Ind]onesia - Eko Nugroho and "Wayang Bocor"
Eko Nurgoho is one of Indonesia['s] most[ provocative] young artists whose style is a unique mix of Indonesia's rich traditions and popular culture tinged with dark humor. Using[ a] distinctive blend[ of][ high] and low art, Nugroho'[ "]Wayang Bocor" is[ a] contemporary form[ of][ theater] in which puppets and actors weave together traditional elements of Indonesian 'wayag' (shadow pupp[ets]) with live theater and scripts that cast a satiric view of contemporary subjects. The show "[God] Bliss["] tells the story[ of] how Islam came to Java, and became absorbed as[ part][ of] J[avan]ese culture that includes elements of Hinduism[,] Buddhism, and animism[.] Simultaneously playful and penetrating.

